first-in-human study as a potential treatment for certain types of epilepsy and a $7,500 milestone was recognized in the six months ended June 30, 2025. Consideration associated with performance milestones is recognized as revenue using the most likely amount method when it is probable that a significant reversal of the cumulative revenue recognized will not occur.","context":"Collaboration revenue:","section":"Item 1. Financial Statements","block":216,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338244","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001582313","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1582313/000119312526338244/xene-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397.bin","sha256":"e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397"}},{"id":"0e106008eb37f5d3ce647a907e07e9fa9bd503a98fea0763ada3cd588450f448","quote":"In April 2017, the Company acquired azetukalner from 1st Order pursuant to an asset purchase agreement. In August 2020, the Company and 1st Order amended the asset purchase agreement to amend certain definitions in the agreement and to modify the payment schedule for certain milestones. Through June 30, 2026, the Company has paid $2,000 based on progress against these milestones. Future potential payments to 1st Order include up to $6,000 in regulatory milestones. There are no royalty obligations to 1st Order.","context":"Asset purchase agreement with 1st Order Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (“1st Order”):","section":"Item 1. Financial Statements","block":230,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338244","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001582313","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1582313/000119312526338244/xene-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397.bin","sha256":"e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397"}},{"id":"b04b77a5850c2412abcce474fc2df9ad9678260cdc9640c7c9cbefb2c67faf56","quote":"The Company has entered into license and research agreements with third parties that include indemnification provisions that are customary in the industry. These indemnification provisions generally require the Company to compensate the other party for certain damages and costs incurred as a result of third-party claims or damages arising from these transactions.","context":"Guarantees and indemnifications:","section":"Item 1. Financial Statements","block":236,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338244","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001582313","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1582313/000119312526338244/xene-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397.bin","sha256":"e5f7afe4c66372350d3653c4df9804a9aa32ba702ebb798995daa4c01acc0397"}},{"id":"52bdec434626fd30a293d539ccdbb8dc4a0d5651fc94034cf75b7cbeb76cf5cc","quote":"Research and development expenses represent costs incurred to conduct development of our proprietary product candidates and our drug discovery efforts, including any acquired or in-licensed product candidates or technology, and costs to support any partnered product candidates.","context":"Research and Development Expenses","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":358,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338244","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001582313","url":"ht